item.description:
arXiv:2608.23019v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: We prove that if $x\in (X,\Delta,\mathbb{T})$ is a log Fano cone singularity over an uncountable algebraically closed field, and $
u_0$ is a $\mathbb{T}$-invariant valuation with center $x$ and $A_{X,\Delta}(
u_0)<\infty$, then the value $$ \delta(X,\Delta;
u_0):=\inf_{
u\in \mathrm{Val}^{\mathbb{T},*}_{X,
i x}} rac{A_{X,\Delta}(
u)}{S(
u_0;
u)}$$ admits a minimum. The proof uses the generic limit argument. Note that there is a counterexample if we discard the log Fano cone structure.
